  "seen_before": false,
  "matches": [],
  "answer": "I found no earlier ticket in the archive that reports this problem. The closest ones (PowerToys#4560 and #3178) are about the Settings UI not saving the filename format, which is a different problem. Your analysis looks sound. When settings.json is missing, Settings.Reload() saves the defaults. That serialization reads FileNameFormat, which caches _fileNameFormat from the default FileName, and the FileName setter never clears the cache. Treat this as a new bug and file it with your suggested fix: clear _fileNameFormat in the FileName setter and mark FileNameFormat [JsonIgnore]. Until it's fixed, run the CLI once so settings.json is created, or open Image Resizer settings once, and then --filename will work."
 },
